  "evidence": [
    "Current Console amalgam contains76orders/editor methods (wait/disband/sentry/movement/grouping/ability/terraform/base creation and scenario-editor operations) and separate UI/lifetime/virtual callback families. Semantics and named realclass APIs justify source separation; original4C/4D/4Eversus50/51address clusters are corroborating observations, NOT proof of original TU filenames, exact boundary or membership.",
    "Taskconsole-refresh-boundary-oct19 executed its one actual Release source-order control and was rejected: all207body measurements and all10scoped complete emitted families were identical, editor_energy still expanded the three window operations instead of original514880, and unrelated menu_proc.text changed load/reference ordering. Do not repeat this source-order screen or globalOb1, noinline/export, cloned body, functionpointer helper or newflagset.",
    "Authorize moving the complete76existing command/editor definition/envelopes verbatim to console_commands.cpp, retaining every C++ body token, original identity/symbol/span/mode/claim/lesson/history. All207Console original identities are in scope to observe affected callers, header copies and generated lifetime contributions; this is not permission to rewrite unrelated bodies. UI/lifecycle/update_data/set_move manual refresh triples and all nontrivial global construction/destruction remain in console.cpp.",
    "Home command-only private helpers, static literals and independently supported passive builtin command state with their consumers. Preserve their bodies/initializers/bindings exactly. Shared state remains one real definition, declared with its existing type in console_commands.h when needed, not duplicated storage or new fixed-address aliases. Preserve same-class Console method declarations/layout in console.h (not editable), no new bases/members/types or inferred capacity. Report unresolvable external declarations or ownership conflicts before expansion, never stub a recovered callee.",
    "Root CMake registers the new real source unit adjacent to console.cpp and shares the existing Console Oy- source group; no other compile/link/ABI/preparation/framework or measurement-policy change. All public CLI/library APIs remain untouched. Existing generated-symbol facts may only be corrected by the native source writer against fresh physical compiler evidence if lexical emission numbering changes; never hand-edit ORIGINAL or bank/demote claims.",
    "Existing source-fixture tests may adapt only to actual current owner files, preserving their behavioral/damage expectations and immutable historical task baselines. A small test-only source accessor may read the two real compiled owners; it must not synthesize missing bodies, become a recovery CLI/compatibility adapter, hide failures or treat concatenation as a TU compiler witness. New migration tests prove identity/envelope/body/data continuity and actual CMake ownership; no exactness asserted before measurement.",
    "Coordinator owns all Git, source integration/cleanup and leased native compilation. Before adopting, ONE unchanged actual Release control per resulting Console unit measures the whole207identity domain, declared passive data and outside-body residuals; original baseline object is reused, not recompiled. Full fresh application build/link, source/claim/reference checks and relevant host controls follow a positive structural review. Source-only partial work remains isolated. Preserve matching regressions/discoveries for explicit review; no automatic rollback of justified source structure to protect a score.",
    "This rehomes existing complete implementations, not new function coverage. Compile/link success, masked bytes and scoped controls are not whole linked-selection/allocation/ICF/structure/runtime or game acceptance. Existing unknown/refused and historical restoration obligations remain; no baseline reset, exclusion, unbound identity deletion, bug fix or relaxed gate. No more framework work without a demonstrated recovery blocker."
  ],
  "intent": "Separate the coherent76Console command/editor implementations and their private passive dependencies from UI/lifecycle code, restoring original out-of-line UI call boundaries without compiler tricks.",
